Z||000000||RobertVol||05-14-2001||11:46 PM||||I have an 88 GT 5Speed and I am wondering for the people that have had loose transmission mounts, How does it feel? Meaning are there symptoms? What are they?<P>The reason I ask is I have noticed that when I come to a stop and then try to engage the clutch to go I can feel 'something" moving in what feels like the console. IS the cable moving &gt; ? <P>Just thought I would check. I am more than likely replacing the mounts on the entire car but thought I would check and see if my Diagnosis sounds correct? <P>PLus I am trying to hurry up and get to 1000 posts!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>And bored <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P>CLICK BELOW AND SEE OUR SITE !!! <BR>NEXT MEETING - May 26th, in Jacksonville<BR><A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fldevel||05-15-2001||12:38 PM|||| i wouldent drive a fiero to long with bad mounts .. could end up verry expensive sence the tranny sits just above the engine cradle when u have bad mounts the trans tend to bounce off that peice of steal just below it usualy resulting in a cracked tranny wich in turn al the oil leaks out of the tranny causeing it to run low on oil wich causes the syncronizers to tighten up wich makes it hard to put in gear "usualy 1st and 3rd" <P> tell me if im getting close  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
